arr[1][0][0] = 6   arr[1][0][1] = 7   
arr[1][1][0] = 8   arr[1][1][1] = 9   
arr[1][2][0] = 10   arr[1][2][1] = 11   How 3D Arrays are Stored in the Memory?Like 2D arrays, the elements of a 3D array should also be stored contiguously in memory.3D ArraySince computer memory is linear, a 3-D array is also stored in a linear form. It can be stored using row-major or column-major order with an additional depth dimension.The array is stored layer by layer (one 2-D array at a time). Within each layer, elements are stored according to the chosen row-major or column-major order.Passing 3D Arrays to FunctionsPassing a 3D array to a function in C is similar to passing 2D arrays, but with an additional dimension. When passing a 3D array, you need to pass the sizes of all the dimensions separately because the size information of array is lost while passing.
